# React Frontend Conventions

## State Management (Zustand)
All global state lives in `src/store/index.ts`. Add new state slices there.
```tsx
// Reading state
const { currentVideo, setPlaying } = useStore()

// Avoid reading the whole store — select only what you need to prevent re-renders
```

## Tauri API Usage
```tsx
import { invoke } from '@tauri-apps/api/core'
import { listen } from '@tauri-apps/api/event'
import { convertFileSrc } from '@tauri-apps/api/core'
import { open, save } from '@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog'
```

### Local file URLs — always use helpers
```tsx
import { getThumbnailSrc, getVideoSrc } from '@/lib/utils'

// ✅ Correct
<img src={getThumbnailSrc(video.thumbnail_path)} />
<video src={convertFileSrc(video.path)} />

// ❌ Wrong — breaks on macOS
<img src={`asset://${path}`} />
```

### IPC timing guard (dev HMR safety)
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const t = setTimeout(() => {
    invoke<MyType>('command_name', { arg }).then(setData).catch(console.warn)
  }, 50)
  return () => clearTimeout(t)
}, [])
```

## Component Patterns
- Modals use `if (!showXxxModal) return null` — they stay mounted in the tree but render nothing
- Modal state is always reset in a `useEffect` on the open flag:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!showModal) return
  // reset local state here
  setError(null)
  setMyList(videos.filter(v => selectedVideoIds.has(v.id)))
}, [showModal])
```

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS v4 — configured via `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin (no `tailwind.config.js`)
- Dark-only app — base colors defined as CSS vars in `src/index.css`
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class names (wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`)
- Avoid mixing Tailwind border/opacity classes with inline `style` — use inline style for dynamic colors

## Path Alias
`@/` maps to `src/` — always use this instead of relative `../../` imports.
